---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Pricing"
  description="Sooppiy subscription plans, billing terms, refund policy and cancellation."
  lastUpdated="August 5, 2026"
>

<div class="legal-notice">
  <p>
    Every new account starts with 7 days of the Junior plan free — no payment
    method required, and nothing is charged when the trial ends. Automation
    simply pauses until you choose a plan.
  </p>
</div>

<h2>Plans</h2>

<div class="plan-scroll">
  <table class="plans">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Plan</th>
        <th>Price</th>
        <th>Free trial</th>
        <th>What it includes</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">Junior</th>
        <td><strong>$60</strong><span class="per">/month</span></td>
        <td><span class="pill pill-on">7 days</span></td>
        <td>Spot markets, manual trading, signals, and the $100,000 simulated paper ledger. Runs on the platform's default AI; no AI Analyst.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">Pro</th>
        <td><strong>$250</strong><span class="per">/month</span></td>
        <td><span class="pill">—</span></td>
        <td>Everything in Junior, plus futures and leverage, the AI Analyst, and your own AI provider by API key.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">Professional</th>
        <td><strong>$500</strong><span class="per">/month</span></td>
        <td><span class="pill">—</span></td>
        <td>Everything in Pro, plus multi-symbol Full Auto fleets — the complete automation desk.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">Enterprise</th>
        <td><strong>Contact us</strong></td>
        <td><span class="pill">—</span></td>
        <td>Custom limits and terms by contract.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<p class="fine">
  Prices are in US dollars, exclusive of tax. Any applicable VAT, GST or
  sales tax is calculated and shown by our payment provider at checkout.
  Accepted payment methods are shown on the subscribe page and may include
  card (including Apple Pay and Google Pay), PayPal, USDT, and bank
  transfer.
</p>

<h2>Free trial</h2>
<p>
  Every new account automatically receives a <strong>7-day free trial</strong>
  of the <strong>Junior</strong> plan. <strong>No payment method is
  required</strong>, and the trial never converts into a paid subscription:
  nothing is charged during the trial and nothing is charged when it ends.
  On day 8 your automation is paused and the subscribe page opens; access
  resumes when you choose a plan.
</p>
<p>
  The trial is limited to <strong>one per account</strong> and is provided on
  the Junior plan only. Pro and Professional bill from the first day.
  Subscribing during the trial ends the trial and begins your paid period
  immediately.
</p>

<h2>Billing and renewal</h2>
<p>
  Subscriptions are billed <strong>monthly in advance</strong>. Card and
  PayPal subscriptions renew automatically on each billing date until you
  cancel; USDT and bank-transfer payments buy a single 30-day period and do
  not renew by themselves. You can change plans at any time: upgrades take
  effect immediately (on the USDT/bank rails you pay only the prorated
  difference for the days remaining), and downgrades take effect at your
  next billing date. If a card payment fails, our payment provider will
  retry it; if it keeps failing, access ends when the paid period expires.
</p>

<h2>Refunds</h2>
<p>
  <strong>Subscription fees are non-refundable, and unused time is not
  pro-rated.</strong>
</p>
<p>
  Sooppiy is not a passive content service. From the moment a billing period
  begins, the platform spends money on your behalf that it cannot recover:
  paid AI model inference for your research, decisions and verifications;
  licensed market, news and sentiment data; and continuous compute for your
  automation runs, monitoring and alerting. Those costs are consumed as you
  use the service. Specifically:
</p>
<ul>
  <li>No refund is given for a billing period that has started — used or unused, whole or partial.</li>
  <li>Cancelling mid-period does not refund, credit or pro-rate the remaining days. Access continues to the end of the period you already paid for.</li>
  <li>Downgrading applies at the next billing cycle; the difference for the current period is not refunded.</li>
  <li>Not using the service during a period is not grounds for a refund.</li>
</ul>
<p>
  The 7-day free trial exists so you can evaluate the platform fully before
  any charge is made. We do refund duplicate or clearly erroneous charges and
  charges arising from confirmed fraudulent use of a payment method, and we
  may credit periods materially affected by an extended outage. Nothing here
  limits rights you have under consumer-protection law that cannot be waived.
</p>

<h2>Cancellation</h2>
<p>
  <strong>You can cancel at any time.</strong> Cancelling stops the next
  renewal — it does not end the period you have already paid for. Your
  access, automation runs and alerts continue until the end of that period,
  after which the account returns to an unsubscribed state.
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Card:</strong> Manage subscription → billing portal → cancel.</li>
  <li><strong>PayPal:</strong> Manage subscription → cancel auto-renewal.</li>
  <li><strong>USDT / bank transfer:</strong> nothing renews by itself — a period simply ends unless you pay for another.</li>
  <li><strong>During the free trial:</strong> there is nothing to cancel — no payment method is on file and the trial simply ends.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Export your data before you cancel</h2>
<div class="legal-notice">
  <p>
    Your trading history, run journals, decision logs, positions, P&amp;L
    records and research outputs can only be viewed and exported while your
    subscription is active. Export them before your access ends.
  </p>
</div>
<p>
  Once access ends you can no longer export your data yourself. High-resolution
  operational data is also deleted on a rolling retention schedule regardless
  of subscription status, and it cannot be reconstructed — not by support, and
  not by subscribing again. Re-subscribing restores your account, but not data
  that has already aged out. If you skip the export, the loss is permanent.
</p>

<h2>Questions</h2>
<p>
  Billing questions go to <a href="mailto:support@sooppiy.com">support@sooppiy.com</a>.
  The full terms are in our <a href="/termsconditions">Terms and Conditions</a>
  — section 8 covers subscriptions, fees and refunds.
</p>

</LegalLayout>

<style>
.plan-scroll { overflow-x: auto; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
table.plans {
  width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; min-width: 560px;
  font-size: .9375rem; color: var(--text-2);
}
table.plans th, table.plans td {
  border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,.08);
  padding: .875rem .75rem; text-align: left; vertical-align: top;
  line-height: 1.6;
}
table.plans thead th {
  font-size: .72rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .1em;
  text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--text-muted);
  border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,.16);
}
table.plans tbody th[scope='row'] {
  font-weight: 700; color: var(--text); white-space: nowrap;
}
table.plans td strong { color: var(--text); font-weight: 700; }
.per { color: var(--text-muted); font-size: .8125rem; margin-left: .15rem; }
.pill {
  display: inline-block; font-size: .75rem; font-weight: 600;
  padding: .15rem .5rem; border-radius: 999px;
  background: rgba(0,0,0,.05); color: var(--text-muted);
}
.pill-on { background: var(--accent-soft); color: var(--accent-h); }
.fine { font-size: .8125rem !important; color: var(--text-muted) !important; }
</style>
